<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>PHP YARA Vulnerability Scanner v3 – CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (Linux)</Title>
    <Description>&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
.phpScan {font-family:Segoe UI,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#243447;max-width:1000px;margin:8px 12px 20px;}
.phpScan h2 {font-size:20px;color:#183953;margin:0 0 5px;}
.phpScan h3 {font-size:15px;color:#183953;margin:20px 0 8px;padding-bottom:5px;border-bottom:2px solid #dbe5ed;}
.phpScan p {margin:7px 0;}
.phpScan .recommend {background:#edf5fa;border-left:4px solid #28658a;padding:10px 12px;margin:12px 0;}
.phpScan table {width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;margin:8px 0;}
.phpScan th {background:#edf1f5;text-align:left;font-weight:600;}
.phpScan td,.phpScan th {padding:8px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #dce3e9;word-wrap:break-word;}
.phpScan .setting {width:31%;}.phpScan .value {width:18%;}
.phpScan .mode {width:110px;}.phpScan .deep {background:#fff7e7;}
.phpScan .warning {color:#865000;font-weight:bold;}
.phpScan input,.phpScan select,.phpScan button {font-family:inherit;font-size:13px;}
.phpScan input {max-width:95%;}.phpScan input[type=text],.phpScan input:not([type]) {box-sizing:border-box;padding:5px;border:1px solid #9baab7;}
.phpScan select {padding:5px;max-width:100%;}.phpScan input[type=checkbox] {margin-top:3px;}
.phpScan .exclusion input {display:block;width:98%;margin:5px 0;}
.phpScan .hint {color:#516170;font-size:12px;}
.phpScan code {font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;word-wrap:break-word;}
.phpScan .launch {border-top:1px solid #dce3e9;padding-top:12px;margin-top:15px;}
.phpScan button {background:#245b7d;color:white;border:1px solid #194766;padding:8px 16px;cursor:pointer;}
.phpScan button:focus,.phpScan input:focus,.phpScan select:focus {outline:2px solid #438bb7;outline-offset:1px;}
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;div class="phpScan"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;PHP vulnerability scan&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Find PHP runtime versions affected by &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109618&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109619&lt;/strong&gt; on Linux, without running PHP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Use the v3 scanners with the v3 Results Analysis. Scanner and Analysis versions should match. Run a new scan after upgrading to refresh the results.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="recommend"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended: start with Quick Scan and leave the limits at their defaults.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Choose a broader scan only when needed. More coverage increases disk activity and run time.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Document, media, font, ordinary text and selected asset file types are skipped in every scan type, including Deep. Native executables and libraries remain eligible; php-config and php_version.h are retained when PHP build-text detection is enabled. A runtime renamed with an excluded extension can be missed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;1. Choose a scan type&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanPreset"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scan type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/label&gt; &lt;select id="PHPScanPreset" onchange="PhpScan.preset(this.value);"&gt;&lt;option value="quick" selected="selected"&gt;QUICK SCAN (recommended)&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="normal"&gt;NORMAL SCAN&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="deep"&gt;DEEP SCAN&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="custom" disabled="disabled"&gt;CUSTOM (advanced settings)&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="mode" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Scan&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Coverage and tradeoff&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quick&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Standard PHP runtime names in the usual application locations. Fastest; can miss renamed or embedded runtimes.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 10 min search; 10 min content scan; 5 million files; 30 GiB candidate input; 512 MiB per file; 10% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Normal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Also checks renamed/nonstandard binaries, while keeping the usual folder exclusions. Broader runtime coverage; takes longer.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 30 min search; 30 min content scan; 10 million files; 40 GiB candidate input; 512 MiB per file; 10% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr class="deep"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Also includes normally skipped OS/cache/data locations and PHP build text. &lt;span class="warning"&gt;WARNING: This takes much longer and is more likely to hit file and scan limits. Deep already uses the maximum search time, content scan time, file count and total candidate input; it can still hit limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 60 min search; 60 min content scan; 10 million files; 100 GiB candidate input; 1 GiB per file; 25% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Choosing a scan type fills its recommended limits below. Quick and Normal use 512 MiB per file and 10% YARA CPU. Deep uses 1 GiB per file and 25% YARA CPU, with the maximum allowed time, file-count and candidate-input budgets. You can adjust individual settings afterward. Remote storage, cloud placeholders and other permanent exclusions still apply. Build text alone does not prove an installed vulnerable runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;2. Advanced settings (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Changing coverage or a preset limit updates the scan type above; a non-preset combination is shown as Custom. Choosing another scan type resets these settings to its recommended values. Additional directory exclusions are retained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="setting" /&gt;&lt;col class="value" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"&gt;Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Scans other native binary names; leaving this off can miss renamed or custom embedded PHP.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"&gt;Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Restores OS, recovery, cache and data locations normally excluded, while retaining scan limits.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBuildText"&gt;Include PHP source/build text (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBuildText"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Includes PHP build/header evidence without treating it as an installed runtime.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Time and resource limits&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="setting" /&gt;&lt;col class="value" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPEnumerationSeconds"&gt;File search time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPEnumerationSeconds" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stops searching after this many minutes and marks unfinished coverage as partial. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanSeconds"&gt;Content scan time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPScanSeconds" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Limits YARA content scanning to this many minutes and reports partial results if it times out. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFiles"&gt;Maximum files checked&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFiles" value="5000000" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps files considered during discovery to bound work on unusually large filesystems. (Allowed: 1000 to 10000000.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCandidateGB"&gt;Maximum candidate input (GiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCandidateGB" value="30" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps the combined size of files sent to YARA; exceeding this reports a partial scan. (Allowed: 1 to 100.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFileMB"&gt;Maximum individual file size (MiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFileMB" value="512" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Skips individual files at or above this size; 512 MiB covers normal PHP and large embedded builds. (Allowed: 16 to 2048.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCpuLimit"&gt;YARA CPU setting (%)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCpuLimit" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sets the YARA engine CPU target; this is not a total system CPU guarantee. (Allowed: 1 to 50.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Additional directory exclusions (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class="exclusion"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;label for="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"&gt;Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;input id="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" value="" size="48" maxlength="4096" /&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Skip your chosen folders; leave blank for no additional exclusions. See the examples below.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What is skipped&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/data/*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The named directory and all its subdirectories.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/data/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\folder\&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Only files directly in that directory; subdirectories are still searched.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;*/data/*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;*\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Every matching directory and its subdirectories, wherever found.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Separate entries with commas, without quotes. Use an absolute path or a leading */; * includes path separators and other characters are literal. Windows ignores case; Linux/macOS matching is case-sensitive. Spaces are supported; commas inside a folder name are not. Maximum 32 entries and 4096 UTF-8 bytes. Exclusions apply to every scan type, can hide PHP, and are logged; intentional exclusions do not mark a scan partial.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="launch"&gt;&lt;button onclick="return PhpScan.prepare();"&gt;Configure and Take Action&lt;/button&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Opens the standard Console Take Action dialog, where you select computers. These settings apply only to that action. API/WebUI actions without parameters use Quick defaults; API integrations can supply the same parameters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Reading the results&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="mode" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;An upstream-affected PHP runtime was found. Check vendor patch status and web exposure before deciding remediation.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FALSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;No affected runtime was found within the completed, selected scan scope.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UNKNOWN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;A short reason identifies unavailable results, incomplete coverage or evidence that needs verification. Vendor backports require checking the package advisory.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;Positive findings are retained during a partial scan. BigFix action success includes usable partial results or no PHP found; failure means no new usable result. The four Analysis properties retain the previous finished result while a scan runs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Coverage and requirements&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quick checks php, php-cgi, php-fpm, phpdbg, lsphp, frankenphp, libphp and mod_php name families, including version suffixes and native runtime libraries (.exe/.dll on Windows, .so/.so.N on Linux, .dylib/.so on macOS). PHP core DLLs and server modules are included. Ordinary .php application scripts do not identify an installed runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Legitimate per-user applications remain in scope, including common PHP installations such as Herd, Scoop, Homebrew, MAMP and XAMPP where applicable. OS/recovery trees, caches, backups and personal data are skipped unless broader locations are selected. Network storage, cloud-only files, symlinks, snapshots and scanner/cache data remain excluded. Archives and container images are not unpacked. Meaningful access restrictions and limits produce partial coverage; the scanner does not change system access or privacy settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux x86-64 or ARM64: RHEL, Rocky, AlmaLinux, Ubuntu, Debian, SUSE/openSUSE, Oracle Linux, Amazon Linux and Fedora; applicability has no distribution-name restriction. Requires Bash 4+, GNU find/coreutils, awk, tar/gzip and flock. Missing prerequisites are reported; nothing is installed automatically.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Minimum ActionScript syntax: BigFix Client 9.5.7. Use a client supported on the target OS and architecture; this syntax minimum does not establish ARM64 support. The pinned YARA-X engine is delivered by BigFix. No endpoint Python, PHP or compiler is required.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Detailed scan log&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;code&gt;YARA_PHP/scan.log&lt;/code&gt; under the BigFix client state root:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;/var/opt/BESClient/YARA_PHP/scan.log&lt;/code&gt; (Linux)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;summary.txt supplies the four Analysis properties; scan.lock prevents overlapping scans. Temporary action work is removed after completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Community utility, not HCL-supported patch content. Rule source: &lt;a href="https://github.com/bigfix/Site_Rapid_Response"&gt;Site Rapid Response&lt;/a&gt; (Apache-2.0).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;var phpScanFields = [{"key": "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex", "label": "Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)", "text": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "label": "Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "label": "Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBuildText", "label": "Include PHP source/build text (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPEnumerationSeconds", "label": "File search time (minutes)", "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60}, {"key": "PHPScanSeconds", "label": "Content scan time (minutes)", "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60}, {"key": "PHPMaxFiles", "label": "Maximum files checked", "min": 1000, "max": 10000000}, {"key": "PHPCandidateGB", "label": "Maximum candidate input (GiB)", "min": 1, "max": 100}, {"key": "PHPMaxFileMB", "label": "Maximum individual file size (MiB)", "min": 16, "max": 2048}, {"key": "PHPCpuLimit", "label": "YARA CPU setting (%)", "min": 1, "max": 50}];
var phpScanWindows = false;
/* Console JScript compatible: no JSON dependency, eval, credentials or target selection. */
var PhpScan = (function () {
    function parameters(values) {
        var fields = phpScanFields, selected = {}, index, field, text, number, multiplier, minimum, maximum;
        for (index = 0; index &lt; fields.length; index++) {
            field = fields[index];
            text = String(values[field.key]);
            if (field.text) {
                // Encode UTF-8 bytes, never interpolate a directory into script code.
                if (/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/.test(text)) { throw new Error('Exclusions cannot contain control characters.'); }
                var entries = text.split(','), clean = [], j, entry, encoded, hex = 'x', k, byte;
                for (j = 0; j &lt; entries.length; j++) {
                    entry = entries[j].replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
                    if (!entry) { continue; }
                    var prefix = phpScanWindows ? /^([A-Za-z]:[\\\/]|\*[\\\/])/ : /^(\/|\*\/)/;
                    var relative = phpScanWindows ? /(^|[\\\/])\.{1,2}([\\\/]|$)/ : /(^|\/)\.{1,2}(\/|$)/;
                    if (!prefix.test(entry) || relative.test(entry)) {
                        throw new Error('Use absolute exclusion paths or a leading */; . and .. segments are not allowed.');
                    }
                    clean.push(entry);
                }
                if (clean.length &gt; 32) { throw new Error('Use at most 32 directory exclusions.'); }
                encoded = encodeURIComponent(clean.join(','));
                for (k = 0; k &lt; encoded.length; k++) {
                    if (encoded.charAt(k) === '%') { byte = encoded.substr(k + 1, 2); k += 2; }
                    else { byte = encoded.charCodeAt(k).toString(16); if (byte.length &lt; 2) { byte = '0' + byte; } }
                    hex += byte.toLowerCase();
                }
                if (hex.length &gt; 8193) { throw new Error('Directory exclusions must fit within 4096 UTF-8 bytes.'); }
                selected[field.key] = hex;
                continue;
            }
            if (!/^[0-9]{1,9}$/.test(text)) { throw new Error(field.label + ': enter a whole number.'); }
            number = Number(text);
            multiplier = field.multiplier || 1;
            minimum = Math.ceil(field.min / multiplier);
            maximum = Math.floor(field.max / multiplier);
            if (number &lt; minimum || number &gt; maximum) { throw new Error(field.label + ': use ' + minimum + ' to ' + maximum + '.'); }
            number = number * multiplier;
            selected[field.key] = String(number);
        }
        return selected;
    }
    function prepare() {
        try {
            var values = {}, index, field;
            for (index = 0; index &lt; phpScanFields.length; index++) {
                field = phpScanFields[index];
                values[field.key] = field.checkbox ? (document.getElementById(field.key).checked ? '1' : '0') : document.getElementById(field.key).value;
            }
            var selected = parameters(values);
            if (typeof TakeFixletAction === 'undefined' || typeof Relevance === 'undefined') {
                throw new Error('Open this content in the BigFix Console to use this settings form. API/WebUI launches use defaults unless action parameters are supplied.');
            }
            // These are ordinary, nonsecret action parameters. The Console
            // obtains the current Task's Action1; no XML or script is rebuilt.
            TakeFixletAction(Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), 'Action1', selected);
        } catch (error) { alert('Cannot prepare scan. ' + error.message); }
        return false;
    }
    var presetFields = ["PHPEnumerationSeconds", "PHPScanSeconds", "PHPMaxFiles", "PHPCandidateGB", "PHPMaxFileMB", "PHPCpuLimit", "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "PHPIncludeBuildText"];
    var presetValues = {"quick": [10, 10, 5000000, 30, 512, 10, false, false, false], "normal": [30, 30, 10000000, 40, 512, 10, true, false, false], "deep": [60, 60, 10000000, 100, 1024, 25, true, true, true]};
    function preset(value) {
        var values = presetValues[value], i, field;
        if (!values) { return; }
        for (i = 0; i &lt; presetFields.length; i++) {
            field = document.getElementById(presetFields[i]);
            if (i &lt; 6) { field.value = String(values[i]); }
            else { field.checked = values[i]; }
        }
        document.getElementById('PHPScanPreset').value = value;
    }
    function syncPreset() {
        var modes = ['quick','normal','deep'], mode, values, i, matches, selected = 'custom', field;
        for (mode = 0; mode &lt; modes.length; mode++) {
            values = presetValues[modes[mode]];
            matches = true;
            for (i = 0; i &lt; presetFields.length; i++) {
                field = document.getElementById(presetFields[i]);
                if (i &lt; 6 ? String(field.value) !== String(values[i]) : field.checked !== values[i]) {
                    matches = false;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (matches) { selected = modes[mode]; break; }
        }
        document.getElementById('PHPScanPreset').value = selected;
    }
    return {parameters: parameters, prepare: prepare, preset: preset, syncPreset: syncPreset};
}());
document.body.ontakeaction = function () { return PhpScan.prepare(); };
&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Action scheduling:&lt;/strong&gt; This action stays Running until the scan finishes and can delay other BigFix actions on that system. File search and content scan have separate time limits; their allowed times add together, plus a short shutdown allowance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;API-only PHP extension markers are logged as supporting evidence; they do not by themselves make a scan UNKNOWN.&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
    <Relevance>if (version of client &gt;= "9.5.7") then (if (name of operating system as lowercase starts with "linux") then ((architecture of operating system = "x86_64" or architecture of operating system = "aarch64") and exists file "/bin/bash") else false) else false</Relevance>
    <Category>PHP Security Discovery</Category>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to run bounded local PHP discovery.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">begin prefetch block
if {architecture of operating system = "aarch64"}
add prefetch item name=yara-x-v1.22.0-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz sha1=fde88001e579387275f731387963dd220f7a6fbd sha256=b1b90f0686ae3e9f607c07b743fd96d6283d9ea5e2fd764919b8505de8b63d4e size=9252173 url=https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/download/v1.22.0/yara-x-v1.22.0-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz
elseif {architecture of operating system = "x86_64"}
add prefetch item name=yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz sha1=f6e1f286242753e0e621c43da7f0c753c8ffc1f4 sha256=7f470770b2c1a0d97f02298fc194978d999074d147d003d33dd62775761439db size=10347394 url=https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/download/v1.22.0/yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz
endif
end prefetch block
action uses file encoding UTF-8 NoBOM
if {architecture of operating system = "aarch64"}
parameter "PHPYaraArchive" = "yara-x-v1.22.0-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz"
parameter "PHPYaraArchiveSha256" = "b1b90f0686ae3e9f607c07b743fd96d6283d9ea5e2fd764919b8505de8b63d4e"
parameter "PHPYaraEngineSha256" = "9839f9b12c45a5ce2b2f0a1672ec06647e604a98738ccbe86c6d43f42a579a0f"
elseif {architecture of operating system = "x86_64"}
parameter "PHPYaraArchive" = "yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz"
parameter "PHPYaraArchiveSha256" = "7f470770b2c1a0d97f02298fc194978d999074d147d003d33dd62775761439db"
parameter "PHPYaraEngineSha256" = "73656c1f7b48326ddad393166a3ed14479412246bd3fe804abe6bf8ff1e6b43f"
else
continue if {false}
endif
if {not exists parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = "x"
endif
continue if {length of parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" &lt;= 8193 and parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = regex "x([0-9A-Fa-f][0-9A-Fa-f])*"}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"}
parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds"}
parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = "600"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPScanSeconds"}
parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = "600"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPScanSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFiles"}
parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = "5000000"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFiles" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &gt;= 1000 and (parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &lt;= 10000000}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCandidateGB"}
parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = "30"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCandidateGB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &lt;= 100}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFileMB"}
parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = "512"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &gt;= 16 and (parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &lt;= 2048}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCpuLimit"}
parameter "PHPCpuLimit" = "10"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCpuLimit" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCpuLimit" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCpuLimit" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCpuLimit" as integer) &lt;= 50}
parameter "output" = "{pathname of parent folder of data folder of client}/YARA_PHP"
// Each attempt owns a separate workspace; interrupted children keep their scan lock.
parameter "work" = "{parameter "output"}/work-{id of action}-{((now - ("01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000" as time)) / microsecond) as integer as string}-{random integer of 2147483647 as string}"
folder create "{parameter "output"}"
folder create "{parameter "work"}"
delete __createfile
createfile until END_PHP_YARA_0f68f1276f3d50db
/*
  PHP install detection + version, all OSes (Linux ELF, Windows PE, macOS Mach-O).

  Deliberately broad: PHP_Binary_Broad flags anything that looks PHP-related so
  nothing is missed; the other rules carry the exact version string. Run with
  `yara -s` (or `yr scan -s`) to print the matched version text.

  Rules:
    PHP_Runtime_Version     - PHP core runtime; $ver holds the exact version,
                              incl. distro suffix (e.g. 8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    PHP_Windows_VersionInfo - any PE whose version resource says ProductName=PHP
                              (php.exe, php-cgi.exe, php8ts.dll, ext\php_*.dll);
                              $pv holds ProductVersion
    PHP_Binary_Broad        - catch-all: any executable with any PHP marker
    PHP_Build_Artifact      - php-config / php_version.h left by source installs

  No modules are imported so the rules also work in embedded YARA engines
  (osquery, EDRs) that are built without the pe/elf/macho modules.

  See README.md for tested samples and the API number -&gt; branch table.
*/

private rule PHP_Detect_IsExecutable
{{
  condition:
    uint32(0) == 0x464C457F                                 // ELF
    or uint16(0) == 0x5A4D                                  // PE (MZ)
    or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACF   // Mach-O 32/64
    or uint32(0) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(0) == 0xCFFAEDFE   // Mach-O 32/64, byte-swapped
    or uint32(0) == 0xBEBAFECA                              // Mach-O universal (CAFEBABE)
}

rule PHP_Runtime_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "PHP core runtime (CLI/CGI/FPM/mod_php/libphp/php*ts.dll/php8.dll/embedded); $ver = exact version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Compile-time literal "X-Powered-By: PHP/" PHP_VERSION in main/SAPI.c.
    // Present regardless of expose_php. Suffix covers distro builds (8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    // and pre-releases (8.5.0RC1).
    $ver = /X-Powered-By: PHP\/[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}/
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and $ver
}

rule PHP_Windows_VersionInfo
{{
  meta:
    description = "Windows PE with PHP version resource; $pv = ProductVersion (exact version)"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // UTF-16LE "ProductName" &lt;NUL + 0-2 bytes alignment pad&gt; "PHP\0"
    $pname = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $pv = /ProductVersion\x00[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.\-]{{0,20}/ wide
  condition:
    // #pv &gt;= 0 is always true: $pv is only there so -s prints the version
    uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and $pname and #pv &gt;= 0
}

rule PHP_Binary_Broad
{{
  meta:
    description = "Broad catch-all: executable containing any PHP runtime/extension marker"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    $xpb    = "X-Powered-By: PHP/"
    $zend   = "Zend Engine v"
    // ZEND_MODULE_BUILD_ID, e.g. API20220829,NTS / API20250925,TS - also in extensions
    $api    = /API20[0-9]{{6},N?TS/
    $pname  = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $grp    = "The PHP Group" ascii wide
    $ini    = "php.ini"
    $fmt    = "PHP %s (%s)"
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and
    (
      $xpb or $zend or $api or $pname
      or ($grp and ($ini or $fmt))
    )
}

rule PHP_Build_Artifact
{{
  meta:
    description = "php-config script or php_version.h header from a PHP build/install; $v* = version"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    // php-config (installed next to the php binary by `make install` and -dev packages)
    $cfg_ver   = /version="[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}"/
    $cfg_a     = "php_cli_binary="
    $cfg_b     = "--php-binary"
    // main/php_version.h
    $hdr_ver   = /#define PHP_VERSION "[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}"/
    $hdr_a     = "#define PHP_MAJOR_VERSION"
  condition:
    filesize &lt; 64KB and
    (
      ($cfg_ver and $cfg_a and $cfg_b)
      or ($hdr_ver and $hdr_a)
    )
}
END_PHP_YARA_0f68f1276f3d50db
delete "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar"
delete __createfile
createfile until END_PHP_YARA_ca5bd8aec1063fab
#!/bin/bash
# Bounded, dependency-light PHP discovery. Bash 4+, GNU find/coreutils, awk,
# tar/gzip and flock (util-linux); no Python, jq, compiler or PHP execution.
# YARA text parsing follows the Apache-2.0 Rapid Response scanner approach.
set -euo pipefail
export LC_ALL=C
umask 077
engine= rules= output= archive= engine_sha256= archive_sha256=
enumeration_seconds=600 scan_seconds=600 max_files=5000000 candidate_gb=30
max_file_mb=512 cpu_limit=10 include_build_text=0 include_broader_locations=0 include_nonstandard_names=0
roots=()

valid_utf8() {{
    local text=$1 i byte remaining=0 low=128 high=191
    for ((i=0;i&lt;${{#text};i++)); do
        printf -v byte '%d' "'${{text:i:1}"
        if ((remaining)); then
            ((byte&gt;=low &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=high)) || return 1
            remaining=$((remaining-1)); low=128; high=191
        elif ((byte&lt;128)); then :
        elif ((byte&gt;=194 &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=223)); then remaining=1
        elif ((byte&gt;=224 &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=239)); then
            remaining=2; ((byte!=224)) || low=160; ((byte!=237)) || high=159
        elif ((byte&gt;=240 &amp;&amp; byte&lt;=244)); then
            remaining=3; ((byte!=240)) || low=144; ((byte!=244)) || high=143
        else return 1; fi
    done
    ((remaining==0))
}
# Shared v3 workspace/path helpers, embedded in both Unix scanners.
cleanup_abandoned_work() {{
    local candidate marker metadata owner mode
    for candidate in "$output"/work-*; do
        [[ -d $candidate &amp;&amp; ! -L $candidate &amp;&amp; $candidate != "$work" ]] || continue
        [[ ${{candidate##*/} =~ ^work-[0-9]+-[0-9]+-[0-9]+$ ]] || continue
        metadata=$(stat -c '%u %a' "$candidate" 2&gt;/dev/null) || continue
        read -r owner mode &lt;&lt;&lt;"$metadata"
        [[ $owner = "$EUID" &amp;&amp; $mode =~ ^[0-7]+$ ]] || continue
        (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || continue
        [[ -f $candidate/attempt.started &amp;&amp; ! -L $candidate/attempt.started ]] || continue
        metadata=$(stat -c '%u %a' "$candidate/attempt.started" 2&gt;/dev/null) || continue
        read -r owner mode &lt;&lt;&lt;"$metadata"
        [[ $owner = "$EUID" &amp;&amp; $mode =~ ^[0-7]+$ ]] || continue
        (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || continue
        marker=
        IFS= read -r marker &lt;"$candidate/attempt.started" || continue
        [[ $marker = PHP_YARA_WORKSPACE_V3 ]] || continue
        # Only a prior launched-v3 workspace is eligible under the global lock.
        # Unmarked folders may still be in ActionScript preparation: leave them.
        rm -rf -- "$candidate"
    done
    [[ ! -L $work/attempt.started ]] || return 1
    printf 'PHP_YARA_WORKSPACE_V3\n' &gt;"$work/attempt.started"
}

scan_list_path_safe() {{
    [[ $1 != *[[:cntrl:]]* ]] || return 1
    [[ $1 != *[!\ -\~]* ]] || valid_utf8 "$1"
}

stage_candidate() {{
    local available blocks copied
    available=$(df -Pk "$work" 2&gt;/dev/null | awk 'NR&gt;1 {{v=$4} END {{if(v ~ /^[0-9]+$/) print v}') || available=
    blocks=$(((size+1023)/1024))
    if [[ ! $available =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || ((available&lt;blocks+65536)); then
        reasons+=('insufficient free space for unusual-path staging')
        return 1
    fi
    # Non-POSIX Bash ulimit -f uses 1024-byte blocks. Bound growing files too.
    if ! (ulimit -f "$blocks"; timeout -k 2 "$((deadline-SECONDS&gt;0 ? deadline-SECONDS : 1))" cp --reflink=auto -- "$path" "$scan_path"); then
        rm -f -- "$scan_path"
        read_errors=$((read_errors+1))
        return 1
    fi
    copied=$(stat -c %s "$scan_path" 2&gt;/dev/null) || copied=
    if [[ $copied != "$size" ]]; then
        rm -f -- "$scan_path"
        read_errors=$((read_errors+1))
        return 1
    fi
}

exclude_directories_hex=x
while (($#)); do
    (($# &gt;= 2)) || {{ echo 'Missing argument' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    case "$1" in
        --engine) engine=$2;; --engine-sha256) engine_sha256=$2;; --rules) rules=$2;; --output) output=$2;;
        --archive) archive=$2;; --archive-sha256) archive_sha256=$2;; --root) roots+=("$2");;
        --enumeration-seconds) enumeration_seconds=$2;; --scan-seconds) scan_seconds=$2;;
        --max-files) max_files=$2;; --candidate-gb) candidate_gb=$2;; --max-file-mb) max_file_mb=$2;;
        --cpu-limit) cpu_limit=$2;; --include-build-text) include_build_text=$2;;
        --include-broader-locations) include_broader_locations=$2;; --include-nonstandard-names) include_nonstandard_names=$2;;
        --exclude-directories-hex) exclude_directories_hex=$2;;
        *) echo 'Unknown argument' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2;;
    esac
    shift 2
done
for name in enumeration_seconds scan_seconds max_files candidate_gb max_file_mb cpu_limit include_build_text include_broader_locations include_nonstandard_names; do
    [[ ${{!name} =~ ^[0-9]{{1,9}$ ]] || {{ echo "Invalid $name" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
done
((enumeration_seconds&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; enumeration_seconds&lt;=3600 &amp;&amp; scan_seconds&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; scan_seconds&lt;=3600 &amp;&amp; max_files&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; max_files&lt;=10000000 &amp;&amp; candidate_gb&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; candidate_gb&lt;=100 &amp;&amp; max_file_mb&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; max_file_mb&lt;=2048 &amp;&amp; cpu_limit&gt;=1 &amp;&amp; cpu_limit&lt;=99 &amp;&amp; include_build_text&lt;=1 &amp;&amp; include_broader_locations&lt;=1 &amp;&amp; include_nonstandard_names&lt;=1)) || {{ echo 'Scan setting outside its allowed range' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
[[ $output = /* &amp;&amp; $engine = /* &amp;&amp; $rules = /* ]] || {{ echo 'Engine, rule and output paths must be absolute' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
missing=()
for command in df find timeout stat od awk sort sha256sum tar gzip flock date mkdir mv chmod dirname mkfifo cp nice cat head tr rm; do
    command -v "$command" &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || missing+=("$command")
done
((${{#missing[@]}==0)) || {{ printf 'Missing required utilities: %s\n' "${{missing[*]}" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
# Reject symlink output ancestors and insecure output ownership. Never change
# permissions on an unrelated directory and never follow an output redirect.
current=$output
while [[ $current != / ]]; do [[ ! -L $current ]] || {{ echo 'Symlink output ancestor rejected' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }; current=${{current%/*}; [[ -n $current ]] || current=/; done
mkdir -p -- "$output"
[[ $(stat -c %u -- "$output") = "$EUID" ]] || {{ echo 'Output directory ownership mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
mode=$(stat -c %a -- "$output"); (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || {{ echo 'Output directory is writable by another account' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
for leaf in scan.lock scan.log scan.log.new summary.txt summary.txt.new; do [[ ! -L $output/$leaf ]] || {{ echo "Symlink output file rejected: $leaf" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }; done
exec 9&gt;"$output/scan.lock"
flock -n 9 || {{ echo 'Another PHP scan is running; retry after it finishes' &gt;&amp;2; exit 75; }
work=$(dirname -- "$engine")
[[ -d $work &amp;&amp; ! -L $work &amp;&amp; $(stat -c %u -- "$work") = "$EUID" ]] || {{ echo 'Unsafe or missing scan workspace' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
mode=$(stat -c %a -- "$work"); (( (8#$mode &amp; 0022)==0 )) || {{ echo 'Scan workspace is writable by another account' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
started=$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC'); start_seconds=$SECONDS
finished=0 find_pid= scan_pid=
failure() {{
    result=$?
    trap - EXIT
    if [[ -n $find_pid ]]; then kill "$find_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; wait "$find_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; fi
    if [[ -n $scan_pid ]]; then kill "$scan_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; wait "$scan_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; fi
    if (( !finished )); then
        printf '\nScan failed (exit %s); previous finished results retained.\n' "$result" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
        if [[ -f $output/summary.txt ]]; then
            awk '/^LAST_SCAN=/{{sub(/ \(Last attempt failed.*/, ""); print $0 " (Last attempt failed; see scan.log)"; next} {{print}' "$output/summary.txt" &gt;"$output/summary.txt.new"
        else printf 'RESULT_FORMAT=2\nDETECTED=UNKNOWN\nLAST_SCAN=NO SCAN (Last attempt failed; see scan.log)\nDURATION=NO SCAN\n' &gt;"$output/summary.txt.new"; fi
        mv -f -- "$output/summary.txt.new" "$output/summary.txt"
    fi
    exit "$result"
}
trap failure EXIT
trap 'exit 130' INT TERM
printf 'PHP scan started: %s\nStandard names: %s; build text: %s; broader locations: %s\n' "$started" "$((1-include_nonstandard_names))" "$include_build_text" "$include_broader_locations" &gt;"$output/scan.log"
exec 2&gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
cleanup_abandoned_work
# Decode only validated byte pairs. Paths are never shell code, printf formats or
# evaluated expressions. GNU find gets quoted regex arguments with literal syntax
# escaped; only '*' is a wildcard. Directory pruning happens before any file read.
[[ ${{#exclude_directories_hex} -le 8193 &amp;&amp; $exclude_directories_hex =~ ^x([0-9a-fA-F]{{2})*$ ]] || {{ echo 'Invalid encoded exclusions' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
exclusion_text=
for ((i=1;i&lt;${{#exclude_directories_hex};i+=2)); do
    pair=${{exclude_directories_hex:i:2}
    [[ $pair != 00 ]] || {{ echo 'NUL in exclusions' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    printf -v character '%b' "\\x$pair"; exclusion_text+=$character
done
[[ $exclusion_text != *[[:cntrl:]]* ]] || {{ echo 'Control character in exclusions' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
custom_trees=(); custom_direct=(); custom_patterns=()
IFS=',' read -r -a exclusion_entries &lt;&lt;&lt;"$exclusion_text"
for pattern in "${{exclusion_entries[@]}"; do
    pattern="${{pattern#"${{pattern%%[![:space:]]*}"}"; pattern="${{pattern%"${{pattern##*[![:space:]]}"}"
    [[ -n $pattern ]] || continue
    ((${{#custom_patterns[@]}&lt;32)) || {{ echo 'At most 32 exclusions allowed' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    [[ $pattern = /* || $pattern = \*/* ]] || {{ echo 'Linux exclusions need an absolute path or leading */' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    [[ ! /$pattern/ =~ /\.\.?/ ]] || {{ echo 'Relative path segments are not allowed' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    while [[ $pattern = *//* ]]; do pattern=${{pattern//\/\//\/}; done
    while [[ $pattern = *\*\** ]]; do pattern=${{pattern//\*\*/\*}; done
    custom_patterns+=("$pattern")
    recursive=0; basis=$pattern
    if [[ $basis = */\* ]]; then recursive=1; basis=${{basis%/\*}; fi
    while [[ $basis = */ ]]; do basis=${{basis%/}; done
    expression=
    for ((i=0;i&lt;${{#basis};i++)); do
        character=${{basis:i:1}
        case "$character" in
            '*') expression+='.*';;
            '.'|'['|']'|'('|')'|'{{'|'}'|'+'|'?'|'^'|'$'|'|'|'\') expression+="\\$character";;
            *) expression+=$character;;
        esac
    done
    if ((recursive)); then custom_trees+=("$expression(/.*)?"); else custom_direct+=("$expression/[^/]+"); fi
    printf 'Custom directory exclusion: %s\n' "$pattern" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
done
hash() {{ sha256sum -- "$1" | awk '{{print $1}'; }
[[ $(hash "$rules") = 0f68f1276f3d50db3dcba06fd1d8089e157fbc8e60bcca49ac1e7b2dde664615 ]] || {{ echo 'Rule hash mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
if [[ ! -f $engine ]]; then
    [[ -f $archive &amp;&amp; $(hash "$archive") = "$archive_sha256" ]] || {{ echo 'Archive hash mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    # Extract only the pinned executable to a controlled filename; no archive paths.
    tar -xOzf "$archive" yr &gt;"$engine"
    chmod 700 -- "$engine"
fi
[[ $(hash "$engine") = "$engine_sha256" ]] || {{ echo 'Engine hash mismatch' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
prune=(/proc /sys /dev /run /var/lib/docker /var/lib/containers /var/lib/containerd /var/lib/rancher /var/lib/lxc /var/lib/lxd /var/snap/lxd /.snapshots /timeshift "$output")
if [[ ${{output##*/} = YARA_PHP ]]; then prune+=("${{output%/*}/__BESData"); fi
if (( !include_broader_locations )); then prune+=(/boot /lost+found /var/log /var/cache /var/backups /var/crash); fi
reasons=()
if ((${{#roots[@]}==0)); then
    # Select an allowed alias before deduplicating bind mounts by device/root.
    # Octal-escaped mount paths are decoded by printf, never by eval.
    declare -A selected_mounts
    while IFS=$'\t' read -r disposition filesystem mount_key mount; do
        printf -v mount '%b' "$mount"
        case "$mount" in *$'\n'*|*$'\r'*|*$'\t'*) echo 'Unusual mount path excluded' &gt;&amp;2; reasons+=('unsupported local filesystem'); continue;; esac
        intentional=0
        for directory in "${{prune[@]}"; do [[ $mount != "$directory" &amp;&amp; $mount != "$directory/"* ]] || intentional=1; done
        for expression in "${{custom_trees[@]}"; do [[ ! $mount =~ ^$expression$ ]] || intentional=1; done
        if ((intentional)); then disposition=EXCLUDED; fi
        if [[ $disposition = SCAN ]]; then
            if [[ ${{selected_mounts[$mount_key]+present} ]]; then disposition=DUPLICATE
            else selected_mounts[$mount_key]=1; fi
        fi
        printf 'Mount: %s | %s | %s\n' "$mount" "$filesystem" "$disposition" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
        case "$disposition" in
            SCAN) roots+=("$mount");;
            UNSUPPORTED) reasons+=('unsupported local filesystem');;
        esac
    done &lt; &lt;(awk '
      {{for(i=7;i&lt;=NF;i++)if($i=="-"){{fs=$(i+1);break}
       key=$3 ":" $4
       if(fs ~ /^(ext[234]|xfs|btrfs|zfs|f2fs|jfs|reiserfs|bcachefs|vfat|exfat|ntfs3)$/ || (fs=="tmpfs" &amp;&amp; ($5=="/tmp" || $5=="/var/tmp"))) {{
         print "SCAN\t" fs "\t" key "\t" $5
       } else if(fs ~ /^(nfs[0-9]*|cifs|smb[0-9]*|9p|ceph|afs|coda|glusterfs|lustre|fuse[.]sshfs|fuse[.]rclone|fuse[.]s3fs|virtiofs)$/) print "REMOTE\t" fs "\t" key "\t" $5
       else if(fs ~ /^(proc|sysfs|devtmpfs|devpts|tmpfs|ramfs|cgroup2?|securityfs|pstore|debugfs|tracefs|configfs|fusectl|mqueue|hugetlbfs|bpf|autofs|binfmt_misc|rpc_pipefs|nsfs|efivarfs)$/) print "SYSTEM\t" fs "\t" key "\t" $5
       else print "UNSUPPORTED\t" fs "\t" key "\t" $5
      }' /proc/self/mountinfo)
fi
((${{#roots[@]})) || {{ echo 'No supported local filesystem found' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
name_expression=( '(' -iname 'php*' -o -iname 'libphp*' -o -iname 'mod_php*' -o -iname 'lsphp*' -o -iname 'frankenphp*' ')' )
((include_nonstandard_names)) &amp;&amp; name_expression=()
prune_expression=( '(' -false )
for directory in "${{prune[@]}"; do prune_expression+=( -o -path "$directory" ); done
prune_expression+=( -o -path '*/.local/share/containers' -o -name '.snapshots' )
for expression in "${{custom_trees[@]}"; do prune_expression+=( -o '(' -type d -regex "$expression" ')' ); done
if ((!include_broader_locations)); then prune_expression+=( -o -path '*/.cache' -o -path '*/.npm/_cacache' -o -path '*/.nuget/packages' ); fi
prune_expression+=( ')' -prune -o )
# File-type scope applies to ALL scan types, including Deep. One case-insensitive
# regex avoids hundreds of find predicates or a child process per file.
non_runtime_extension_regex='.*[.](3g2|3gp|3mf|aac|ai|aif|aifc|aiff|alac|amr|arw|ass|avi|avif|bdf|bib|blend|bmp|c4d|cfg|conf|cr2|cr3|css|csv|dgn|dib|dng|doc|docm|docx|dot|dotm|dotx|dwg|dxf|eml|eot|eps|epub|fbx|flac|flv|fnt|fon|frag|geojson|gif|glb|glsl|gltf|gpx|heic|heif|hlsl|htm|html|icns|ico|ics|iges|igs|indd|inf|ini|jpe|jpeg|jpg|json|jsonl|key|kml|kmz|less|log|m2ts|m2v|m4a|m4b|m4v|ma|manifest|markdown|max|mb|mbox|md|mid|midi|mkv|mobi|mov|mp3|mp4|mpeg|mpg|msg|mts|ndjson|nef|numbers|odp|ods|odt|oga|ogg|ogv|opus|orf|ost|otf|otp|ots|ott|pages|pcf|pdf|png|pot|potm|potx|pps|ppsm|ppsx|ppt|pptm|pptx|prefab|properties|psb|psd|pst|reg|rst|rtf|rw2|sass|scss|shader|shadergraph|shp|shx|sketch|srt|ssa|step|stl|stp|svg|tex|tif|tiff|toml|tsv|ttc|ttf|txt|uasset|ucas|umap|unity|unitypackage|usf|ush|utoc|vcf|vert|vob|vpk|vtt|wav|webm|webp|wma|wmv|woff|woff2|xcf|xhtml|xls|xlsb|xlsm|xlsx|xlt|xltm|xltx|xml|yaml|yml)'
file_scope_expression=( '(' -iname 'php-config' -o -iname 'php_version.h' -o '!' -iregex "$non_runtime_extension_regex" ')' )

direct_expression=()
for expression in "${{custom_direct[@]}"; do direct_expression+=( '!' -regex "$expression" ); done
list=$work/candidates.txt; raw=$work/results.txt; errors=$work/engine.stderr; fifo=$work/find.pipe
# Recovery happens only after acquiring the global scan lock. A prior interrupted
# attempt may leave its FIFO/staging directory; never follow or remove a symlink.
for leaf in candidates.txt results.txt engine.stderr find.stderr versions.tsv vulnerable.txt unverified.txt find.pipe staged; do
    [[ ! -L $work/$leaf ]] || {{ echo "Symlink workspace item rejected: $leaf" &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
done
: &gt;"$list"; : &gt;"$raw"; : &gt;"$errors"
if [[ -e $fifo ]]; then
    [[ -p $fifo ]] || {{ echo 'Unexpected object at discovery FIFO path' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
    rm -f -- "$fifo"
fi
mkfifo -- "$fifo"
mkdir -p -- "$work/staged"
declare -A original_paths
discovery_stopped=0
files=0; candidates=0; bytes=0; size_skipped=0; structural_skipped=0; read_errors=0
deadline=$((SECONDS+enumeration_seconds))
# A timeout covers blocked directory reads. Streaming NUL records preserves path
# bytes and avoids a huge on-disk inventory; the FIFO provides backpressure.
timeout -k 5 "$enumeration_seconds" find "${{roots[@]}" -regextype posix-extended -xdev -ignore_readdir_race "${{prune_expression[@]}" -type f "${{name_expression[@]}" "${{file_scope_expression[@]}" "${{direct_expression[@]}" -printf '%s\0%p\0' &gt;"$fifo" 2&gt;"$work/find.stderr" &amp;
find_pid=$!
while IFS= read -r -d '' -t "$enumeration_seconds" size &amp;&amp; IFS= read -r -d '' -t 5 path; do
    if ((SECONDS&gt;=deadline)); then reasons+=('file search time limit reached'); discovery_stopped=1; break; fi
    if ((files&gt;=max_files)); then reasons+=('file count limit reached'); discovery_stopped=1; break; fi
    files=$((files+1)); leaf=${{path##*/}; lower=${{leaf,,}
    if ((!include_nonstandard_names)); then
        [[ $lower =~ ^(php|phpdbg|libphp|mod_php|lsphp|frankenphp)([0-9][0-9.]*([-_][a-z0-9_.-]+)?|[-_][a-z0-9_.-]+)?(ts|nts|apache[0-9_]*)?(\.exe|\.dll|\.so(\.[0-9]+)*)?$ ]] || continue
        case "$lower" in
            php-config|php_version.h) ((include_build_text)) || continue;;
            *.*) extension=${{lower##*.}; [[ $extension = exe || $extension = dll || $extension = so || $extension =~ ^[0-9][a-z0-9_-]*$ ]] || continue;;
        esac
    fi
    if [[ $lower = php-config || $lower = php_version.h ]]; then ((include_build_text)) || continue; fi
    if ((!include_broader_locations)); then case "$lower" in *.db|*.sqlite|*.sqlite3|*.bak|*.dump|*.dmp|*.iso|*.vhd|*.vhdx|*.vmdk|*.wim|*.esd) continue;; esac; fi
    # Stat/find never opens devices or FIFOs. Recheck after enumeration before
    # reading, because an application can replace its file during a scan.
    [[ -f $path &amp;&amp; ! -L $path ]] || continue
    if ! header=$(timeout -k 1 2 od -An -tx1 -N20 -- "$path" 2&gt;/dev/null | tr -d ' \n'); then
        [[ -e $path ]] &amp;&amp; read_errors=$((read_errors+1)); continue
    fi
    binary=0
    case "$header" in
        7f454c46*)
            # ELF ET_REL/ET_CORE cannot be a live PHP executable/shared runtime.
            elf_type=${{header:32:4}
            if [[ $elf_type = 0100 || $elf_type = 0001 || $elf_type = 0400 || $elf_type = 0004 ]]; then structural_skipped=$((structural_skipped+1)); continue; fi
            binary=1;;
        4d5a*|cefaedfe*|cffaedfe*|feedface*|feedfacf*|cafebabe*) binary=1;;
    esac
    if ((!binary)); then ((include_build_text &amp;&amp; size&lt;65536)) || continue; fi
    # The bounded header check above rejects non-runtime data without reading
    # the full file. Only a plausible candidate skipped by size is a coverage gap.
    if ((size&gt;=max_file_mb*1048576)); then
        size_skipped=$((size_skipped+1))
        if ((size_skipped&lt;=20)); then
            printf 'Size-limited runtime candidate (%s bytes; path capped at 800 bytes): %q\n' "$size" "${{path:0:800}" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
        fi
        continue
    fi
    if ((bytes+size&gt;candidate_gb*1073741824)); then reasons+=('total candidate size limit'); discovery_stopped=1; break; fi
    # YARA scan lists are UTF-8 and newline-separated. Stage unusual raw-byte
    # paths to ASCII names; retain original bytes for readable UTF-8 reporting.
    scan_path=$path
    if ! scan_list_path_safe "$path"; then
        scan_path=$work/staged/$candidates
        [[ ! -L $scan_path ]] || {{ echo 'Symlink staged file rejected' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; }
        stage_candidate || continue
        original_paths["$scan_path"]=$path
    fi
    printf '%s\n' "$scan_path" &gt;&gt;"$list"
    candidates=$((candidates+1)); bytes=$((bytes+size))
done &lt;"$fifo"
if ((discovery_stopped)); then kill "$find_pid" 2&gt;/dev/null || :; fi
find_rc=0; wait "$find_pid" || find_rc=$?; find_pid=
if ((find_rc!=0 &amp;&amp; !discovery_stopped)); then
    if ((SECONDS&gt;=deadline)); then reasons+=('file search time limit reached')
    else reasons+=('file search incomplete'); fi
fi
if [[ -s $work/find.stderr ]]; then reasons+=('unreadable locations'); fi
((size_skipped==0)) || reasons+=('file size limit')
((read_errors==0)) || reasons+=('unreadable files')
if ((candidates)); then
    runner=(nice -n 10)
    # Idle I/O is optional, never a prerequisite that can suppress detection.
    if command -v ionice &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 &amp;&amp; ionice -c 3 true 2&gt;/dev/null; then runner+=(ionice -c 3); fi
    (ulimit -f 65536; exec timeout -k 5 "$((scan_seconds+15))" "${{runner[@]}" "$engine" scan --scan-list --print-strings --output-format text --threads 2 --cpu-limit "$cpu_limit" --timeout "$scan_seconds" --max-matches-per-pattern 64 "$rules" "$list") &gt;"$raw" 2&gt;"$errors" &amp;
    scan_pid=$!; scan_rc=0; wait "$scan_pid" || scan_rc=$?; scan_pid=
    ((scan_rc==0)) || reasons+=('YARA time/output/error limit')
    [[ ! -s $errors ]] || reasons+=('YARA warnings or unreadable files')
fi
# Parse the engine's documented text output, not shell code or executable PHP.
awk '
 /^PHP_/ {{rule=$1; file=$0; sub(/^[^ ]+ /,"",file); seen[file]=1; if(rule=="PHP_Runtime_Version")core[file]=1; if(rule=="PHP_Build_Artifact")build[file]=1; next}
 /:\$[A-Za-z_]+: / {{if(rule=="PHP_Binary_Broad") {{if($0 ~ /:\$api: /) api[file]=1; else non_api[file]=1}}
 /:\$(ver|pv|cfg_ver|hdr_ver): / {{v=$0; gsub(/\\x00/,"",v); sub(/^[^ ]+ /,"",v); if(match(v,/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]*/)) {{v=substr(v,RSTART,RLENGTH); if(rule=="PHP_Runtime_Version")runtime[file SUBSEP v]=1; else evidence[file SUBSEP v]=1}}
 END {{for(k in runtime){{split(k,a,SUBSEP);print a[1] "\truntime\t" a[2]} for(k in evidence){{split(k,a,SUBSEP);if(!core[a[1]])print a[1] "\tevidence\t" a[2]} for(f in seen)if(!core[f] &amp;&amp; !build[f]) print f ((api[f] &amp;&amp; !non_api[f]) ? "\textension_only\tunknown" : "\tunconfirmed\tunknown")}
' "$raw" | sort -u &gt;"$work/versions.tsv"
# Bash 4 can validate UTF-8 without installing a locale, Python or another tool.
# Invalid bytes and control characters use reversible shell quoting, never eval.
display_path() {{
    if [[ $1 != *[[:cntrl:]]* ]] &amp;&amp; valid_utf8 "$1"; then printf '%s' "$1"; else printf '%q' "$1"; fi
}
summary_row() {{
    local row=$1
    if ((${{#row}&gt;900)); then
        row=${{row:0:870}
        while ! valid_utf8 "$row"; do row=${{row%?}; done
        row+='...[full path in scan.log]'
    fi
    printf '%s\n' "$row"
}

# Package ownership is evidence that a vendor may have backported the fix; it
# does not prove patch status. Query only affected findings, cache per path, and
# cap all package lookups together at 30 seconds (at most two seconds per call).
declare -A package_cache
package_deadline=$((SECONDS+30))
package_status() {{
    local file=$1 manager answer rc budget
    if [[ ${{package_cache[$file]+present} ]]; then package_state=${{package_cache[$file]}; return; fi
    package_state=unverified
    # dpkg -S interprets glob syntax even in a quoted argument. Do not let an
    # unusual filename expand the ownership lookup into a package-wide search.
    case "$file" in *'*'*|*'?'*|*'['*|*']'*|*'\'*) package_cache["$file"]=$package_state; return;; esac
    for manager in rpm dpkg-query; do
        command -v "$manager" &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || continue
        budget=$((package_deadline-SECONDS)); ((budget&lt;=2)) || budget=2
        if ((budget&lt;1)); then package_state=unverified; break; fi
        rc=0
        if [[ $manager = rpm ]]; then
            answer=$(timeout -k 1 "$budget" rpm -qf --qf '%{{NAME}-%{{VERSION}-%{{RELEASE}\n' -- "$file" 2&gt;&amp;1 | head -c 8192) || rc=$?
        else answer=$(timeout -k 1 "$budget" dpkg-query -S -- "$file" 2&gt;&amp;1 | head -c 8192) || rc=$?; fi
        if ((rc==0)); then package_state=vendor; break; fi
        if ((rc!=1)) || [[ $answer != *'not owned by any package'* &amp;&amp; $answer != *'no path found matching pattern'* ]]; then package_state=unverified; break; fi
        package_state=unowned
    done
    package_cache["$file"]=$package_state
}
vulnerable=0; unknown=0; findings=0; vendor_unverified=0
: &gt;"$work/vulnerable.txt"; : &gt;"$work/unverified.txt"
while IFS=$'\t' read -r path kind version; do
    [[ -n $path ]] || continue
    findings=$((findings+1))
    original=${{original_paths[$path]-$path}
    display=$(display_path "$original")
    printf 'Finding: %s | %s | PHP %s\n' "$display" "$kind" "$version" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
    if [[ $kind != runtime ]]; then
        # Build evidence is expected only in the opt-in mode. Unknown runtime
        # versions remain a visible qualification in the last-scan property.
        [[ $kind != unconfirmed ]] || unknown=$((unknown+1))
        if [[ $kind = unconfirmed ]]; then printf '%s | PHP version/runtime unconfirmed\n' "$display" &gt;&gt;"$work/unverified.txt"; fi
        continue
    fi
    [[ $version =~ ^([0-9]{{1,2})\.([0-9]{{1,2})\.([0-9]{{1,3})(.*)$ ]] || {{ unknown=$((unknown+1)); printf '%s | PHP version unavailable\n' "$display" &gt;&gt;"$work/unverified.txt"; continue; }
    major=$((10#${{BASH_REMATCH[1]})); minor=$((10#${{BASH_REMATCH[2]})); patch=$((10#${{BASH_REMATCH[3]})); suffix=${{BASH_REMATCH[4]}
    fixed=0 affected=0
    case "$major.$minor" in 8.2) fixed=35;; 8.3) fixed=36;; 8.4) fixed=27;; 8.5) fixed=12;; esac
    if ((fixed)); then
        if ((patch&lt;fixed)) || {{ ((patch==fixed)) &amp;&amp; [[ $suffix =~ ^(alpha|beta|RC|dev) ]]; }; then affected=1; fi
    elif (( (major==5 &amp;&amp; minor&gt;=4) || major==7 || (major==8 &amp;&amp; minor&lt;2) )); then affected=1
    else unknown=$((unknown+1)); printf '%s | PHP %s | Version assessment unavailable\n' "$display" "$version" &gt;&gt;"$work/unverified.txt"; fi
    if ((affected)); then
        package_status "$original"
        if [[ $package_state != unowned || ( -n $suffix &amp;&amp; ! $suffix =~ ^(alpha|beta|RC|dev)[0-9]*$ ) ]]; then
            vendor_unverified=$((vendor_unverified+1))
            printf '%s | PHP %s | Vendor patch status unverified\n' "$display" "$version" &gt;&gt;"$work/unverified.txt"
            printf 'Vendor patch status unverified: %s | ownership %s\n' "$display" "$package_state" &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
        else
            vulnerable=$((vulnerable+1))
            printf '%s | PHP %s\n' "$display" "$version" &gt;&gt;"$work/vulnerable.txt"
        fi
    fi
done &lt;"$work/versions.tsv"
((unknown==0)) || reasons+=('unconfirmed PHP version/runtime')
if ((${{#reasons[@]})); then
    # Multiple unsupported mounts or files can have the same cause; show it once.
    mapfile -t reasons &lt; &lt;(printf '%s\n' "${{reasons[@]}" | sort -u)
fi
elapsed=$((SECONDS-start_seconds))
printf -v duration '%s hours, %s minutes, %s seconds' "$((elapsed/3600))" "$((elapsed%3600/60))" "$((elapsed%60))"
completed=$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC'); last_scan=$completed
if ((${{#reasons[@]})); then
    reason_text=
    for reason in "${{reasons[@]}"; do
        [[ -z $reason_text ]] || reason_text+=', '
        reason_text+=$reason
    done
    last_scan+=" (Partial: $reason_text; see scan.log)"
fi
if ((vendor_unverified)); then last_scan+=' (Vendor patch status unverified; see scan.log)'; fi
if ((vulnerable+vendor_unverified+unknown&gt;100)); then last_scan+=' (first 100 paths shown; all paths in scan.log)'; fi
{{
    printf '\nCompleted: %s\nDuration: %s\nFiles considered: %s\nCandidates: %s\nCandidate bytes: %s\nOver size limit: %s\nRead errors: %s\nStructural skips: %s\nFindings: %s\nUpstream-affected runtime paths: %s\n' "$completed" "$duration" "$files" "$candidates" "$bytes" "$size_skipped" "$read_errors" "$structural_skipped" "$findings" "$vulnerable"
    printf 'Limits: search %ss; YARA %ss; files %s; individual file %s MiB; candidate input %s GiB; CPU %s%%\n' "$enumeration_seconds" "$scan_seconds" "$max_files" "$max_file_mb" "$candidate_gb" "$cpu_limit"
    printf 'Result: %s\n' "$last_scan"
    printf 'Vendor-unverified runtime paths: %s\n' "$vendor_unverified"
    printf 'TRUE: upstream-affected runtime detected. FALSE: none detected within complete scan scope. UNKNOWN: unavailable, incomplete or unverified evidence. Vendor package patch status and web exposure require verification.\n'
    head -c 32768 -- "$work/find.stderr" "$errors"
} &gt;&gt;"$output/scan.log"
{{
    echo RESULT_FORMAT=2
    if ((vulnerable)); then echo DETECTED=TRUE
    elif ((vendor_unverified || unknown || ${{#reasons[@]})); then
        echo DETECTED=UNKNOWN
        unknown_reason=
        for reason in "${{reasons[@]}"; do
            case "$reason" in
                'file size limit') detail="$size_skipped possible runtime file(s) at or above $max_file_mb MiB skipped";;
                'YARA time/output/error limit') detail='Content scan incomplete (time, output or engine error)' ;;
                *) detail=$reason;;
            esac
            [[ -z $unknown_reason ]] || unknown_reason+='; '
            unknown_reason+=$detail
        done
        if ((vendor_unverified)); then
            [[ -z $unknown_reason ]] || unknown_reason+='; '
            unknown_reason+='Vendor patch status unverified'
        fi
        printf 'UNKNOWN_REASON=%s\n' "${{unknown_reason:0:800}"
    else echo DETECTED=FALSE; fi
    printf 'LAST_SCAN=%s\nDURATION=%s\n' "$last_scan" "$duration"
    rows=0
    while IFS= read -r row; do
        ((rows&lt;100)) || break
        summary_row "VULNERABLE=$row"; rows=$((rows+1))
    done &lt;"$work/vulnerable.txt"
    while IFS= read -r row; do
        ((rows&lt;100)) || break
        summary_row "UNVERIFIED=$row"; rows=$((rows+1))
    done &lt;"$work/unverified.txt"
} &gt;"$output/summary.txt.new"
mv -f -- "$output/summary.txt.new" "$output/summary.txt"
finished=1
if ((${{#reasons[@]})); then exit 10; fi
END_PHP_YARA_ca5bd8aec1063fab
delete "{parameter "work"}/scan-linux.sh"
move __createfile "{parameter "work"}/scan-linux.sh"
wait /bin/bash "{parameter "work"}/scan-linux.sh" --engine "{parameter "work"}/yr" --engine-sha256 {parameter "PHPYaraEngineSha256"} --rules "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar" --output "{parameter "output"}" --archive "{pathname of download file (parameter "PHPYaraArchive")}" --archive-sha256 {parameter "PHPYaraArchiveSha256"} --enumeration-seconds {parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds"} --scan-seconds {parameter "PHPScanSeconds"} --max-files {parameter "PHPMaxFiles"} --candidate-gb {parameter "PHPCandidateGB"} --max-file-mb {parameter "PHPMaxFileMB"} --cpu-limit {parameter "PHPCpuLimit"} --exclude-directories-hex "{parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"}" --include-build-text {parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText"} --include-broader-locations {parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"} --include-nonstandard-names {parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"}
parameter "scanExit" = "{exit code of action}"
folder delete "{parameter "work"}"
continue if {parameter "scanExit" = "0" or parameter "scanExit" = "10"}
exit 0
</ActionScript>
      <SuccessCriteria Option="RunToCompletion" />
    </DefaultAction>
  </Task>
</BES>
